- `action(n1, "start")`: Hallucinates an initial step; the source begins directly with "the customer needs to make a purchase".
- `action(n4, "add item to cart / continue shopping")`: Misrepresents a conditional decision point as a sequential action; the source frames this as a branching choice ("If they choose to... if they select...").
- `branch(b1, XOR)` and `defines(v1, ...)`: Lacks guard conditions and declares an empty range `{}`, failing to encode the source-specified selection criteria ("Add item to cart" vs "Continue Shopping").
- `action(n6, "continue shopping")`: Terminates as a dead-end node with no outgoing precedence, contradicting the source instruction that selecting this option means they "should continue with the process".
- `action(n9, "checkout tasks completed?")`, `branch(b2, XOR)`, and `guard(b2, ...)`: Hallucinates an intermediate validation step; the source proceeds directly from the parallel checkout tasks to evaluating credit card and inventory status.
- `action(n10, "credit card approved and inventory in stock?")`: Misclassified as an `action` instead of a `branch`; the source treats this as a conditional gateway determining subsequent flow.
- `defines(v2, ...)` and `defines(v3, ...)`: Specify empty or incomplete ranges `{}` and `{"Checkout Tasks Not Completed"}`, omitting the source-defined evaluation states (approved/denied, in stock/out of stock).
- `branch(b3, XOR)` routing to `action(n16, "transaction ended")` → `end(e2)`: Violates the source directive "In either case, the order confirmation number should be displayed"; the rejection/out-of-stock path terminates immediately instead of converging to execute the mandatory confirmation sequence.
- Missing guards on `branch(b1)` and `branch(b3)`: Critical control-flow transitions lack boolean conditions, leaving the model unable to faithfully evaluate the "Continue Shopping", "approved/in stock", and "denied/no inventory" outcomes described in the source.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n6` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n6,"continue shopping")
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `['Checkout Tasks Not Completed']`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v2 = 'Checkout Tasks Not Completed'` on `b2 -> n17` uses undefined variable `v2`. | DSL: guard(b2,n17,"v2 = 'Checkout Tasks Not Completed'")
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n5` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n10` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n11` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n16` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S5] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: n6 | DSL: action(n6,"continue shopping")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v2 = 'Checkout Tasks Not Completed'` on `b2 -> n17` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b2,n17,"v2 = 'Checkout Tasks Not Completed'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b2` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range.
